    {
      "id": "GCC-02",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-gram-congruence-section",
      "title": "The diagonal square branch selects a continuous congruence section",
      "statement": "There is a subgroup Q of GL_n(K) such that q↦q*Sq embeds Q homeomorphically onto an open neighborhood of S. In diagonal coordinates its image has p_i/d_i in U² for a base-unit subgroup U on which squaring is an open embedding. Its inverse selects q=1 at T=S.",
      "hypotheses": "The parent Gram spaces use fixed conjugation and congruence by * on the left. For R a finite completion of F, 2 is a nonzero field element in every residue characteristic. At real places use the positive branch.",
      "correspondence": "Relative to S=b*Db the subgroup is b⁻¹ L b with L upper triangular and prescribed diagonal group U. The fibre construction precomposes this congruence chart with inversion to define a left action. The explicit ball k>ord(2) illustrates the existential ultrametric neighborhood.",
      "dependencies": [
        "GCC-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-gram-congruence-orbit"
      ],
